IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `act-nouns`
IMPORT `act-interpretation-time`

-- Legislation Act 2001 (Australian Capital Territory), chapter 8: Commencement and exercise of powers before commencement.
--
-- The rules that compute a commencement (ss 73 to 75A, 77 (3) and (4), 79 (1), 81 (6) and (7)) are in `act-interpretation-time.l4`,
-- which also holds the moment-within-the-day rule of s 74 and the points-in-time those rules compare.
-- This module holds the rest of the chapter: the meaning of "law" (s 72), the sections s 73 gives way to (s 73 (5)),
-- when the sections apply (ss 75AA (1), 79 (2), 79A, 81 (1) to (5)), retrospective commencement (ss 75B, 76),
-- commencement notices (s 77 (1), (2)), separate commencement of amendments (s 78), the definitions in s 79 (4), and references to commencement (s 80).
-- The definitions inside these sections are also in `act-section-definitions.l4`.

§ `Legislation Act 2001 (ACT): chapter 8, Commencement`

-- src:983 | In this chapter:
-- src:984 | law means an Act or statutory instrument.
@ref s 72 (src:983-984)
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of Act or instrument`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 72: the kind of document is a law for chapter 8` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `an Act` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a subordinate law` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a disallowable instrument` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a notifiable instrument` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a commencement notice` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a statutory instrument of another kind` THEN TRUE

-- src:1004 | (5) This section is subject to the following sections:
-- src:1005 | (a) section 75 (Commencement of naming and commencement provisions);
-- src:1006 | (b) section 76 (Non-prejudicial provision may commence retrospectively);
-- src:1007 | (c) section 79 (Automatic commencement of postponed law);
-- src:1008 | (d) section 79A (Commencement of amendment of uncommenced law);
-- src:1009 | (e) section 81 (Exercise of powers between notification and commencement).
@ref s 73 (5) (src:1004-1009)
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`s 73 (5): the sections that s 73 is subject to` MEANS LIST "75", "76", "79", "79A", "81"

-- src:1027 | (1) This section applies if a law amends another law and includes a provision (a legislation amended provision) identifying the amended law.
@ref s 75AA (1) (src:1027-1027)
GIVEN aLawAmendsAnotherLaw IS A BOOLEAN, theLawIncludesAProvisionIdentifyingTheAmendedLaw IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 75AA (1): s 75AA applies to the law` MEANS aLawAmendsAnotherLaw AND theLawIncludesAProvisionIdentifyingTheAmendedLaw

-- src:1040 | (1) A law must not be taken to provide for the law (or another law) to commence retrospectively unless the law clearly indicates that it is to commence retrospectively.
@ref s 75B (1) (src:1040-1040)
GIVEN theLawClearlyIndicatesThatItIsToCommenceRetrospectively IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 75B (1): the law is taken to provide for the law (or another law) to commence retrospectively` MEANS theLawClearlyIndicatesThatItIsToCommenceRetrospectively

-- s 76 (4): a prejudicial provision operates to the disadvantage of a person (other than the Territory or a territory authority or instrumentality)
-- by adversely affecting the person's rights or imposing liabilities on the person.
-- src:1059 | prejudicial provision means a provision that operates to the disadvantage of a person (other than the Territory or a territory authority or instrumentality) by—
-- src:1060 | (a) adversely affecting the person’s rights; or
-- src:1061 | (b) imposing liabilities on the person.
@ref s 76 (4), definition of prejudicial provision (src:1059-1061)
GIVEN thePersonIsTheTerritoryOrATerritoryAuthorityOrInstrumentality IS A BOOLEAN, theProvisionAdverselyAffectsThePersonsRights IS A BOOLEAN, theProvisionImposesLiabilitiesOnThePerson IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 76 (4): the provision is a prejudicial provision` MEANS
    (NOT thePersonIsTheTerritoryOrATerritoryAuthorityOrInstrumentality)
    AND (theProvisionAdverselyAffectsThePersonsRights OR theProvisionImposesLiabilitiesOnThePerson)

-- src:1058 | non-prejudicial provision means a provision that is not a prejudicial provision.
@ref s 76 (4), definition of non-prejudicial provision (src:1058-1058)
GIVEN theProvisionIsAPrejudicialProvision IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 76 (4): the provision is a non-prejudicial provision` MEANS (NOT theProvisionIsAPrejudicialProvision)

-- src:1050 | (1) A statutory instrument may provide that a non-prejudicial provision of the instrument commences retrospectively.
@ref s 76 (1) (src:1050-1050)
GIVEN theProvisionIsAPrejudicialProvision IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 76 (1): a statutory instrument may provide that the provision commences retrospectively` MEANS
    IF   NOT theProvisionIsAPrejudicialProvision
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:1051 | (2) Unless this subsection is displaced by, or under authority given by, an Act, a statutory instrument cannot provide that a prejudicial provision of the instrument commences retrospectively.
@ref s 76 (2) (src:1051-1051)
GIVEN theProvisionIsAPrejudicialProvision IS A BOOLEAN, thisSubsectionIsDisplacedByOrUnderAuthorityGivenByAnAct IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 76 (2): a statutory instrument can provide that the prejudicial provision commences retrospectively` MEANS
    IF   theProvisionIsAPrejudicialProvision AND (NOT thisSubsectionIsDisplacedByOrUnderAuthorityGivenByAnAct)
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:1064 | (1) If a law is expressed to commence on a day fixed or otherwise determined by a notice—
-- src:1065 | (a) a single day, or a time on a single day, may be fixed or determined; or
@ref s 77 (1) (a) (src:1064-1065)
GIVEN aLawIsExpressedToCommenceOnADayFixedOrOtherwiseDeterminedByANotice IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 77 (1) (a): a single day, or a time on a single day, may be fixed or determined` MEANS aLawIsExpressedToCommenceOnADayFixedOrOtherwiseDeterminedByANotice

-- src:1066 | (b) different days or times may be fixed or determined for different provisions.
@ref s 77 (1) (b) (src:1066-1066)
GIVEN aLawIsExpressedToCommenceOnADayFixedOrOtherwiseDeterminedByANotice IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 77 (1) (b): different days or times may be fixed or determined for different provisions` MEANS aLawIsExpressedToCommenceOnADayFixedOrOtherwiseDeterminedByANotice

-- src:1067 | (2) A commencement notice for a law is valid even if the day or time fixed or otherwise determined by the notice happens before the notice’s notification day.
@ref s 77 (2) (src:1067-1067)
GIVEN theDayOrTimeFixedHappensBeforeTheNoticesNotificationDay IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 77 (2): the commencement notice for the law is valid` MEANS TRUE

-- src:1076 | (1) Amendments made by a provision of a law may be given separate commencements, whether or not the provision is self-contained.
@ref s 78 (1) (src:1076-1076)
GIVEN theAmendmentsAreMadeByAProvisionOfALaw IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 78 (1): the amendments may be given separate commencements` MEANS theAmendmentsAreMadeByAProvisionOfALaw

-- src:1077 | Examples
-- src:1078 | 1 A provision of an amending law inserts 2 sections. The sections may be given separate commencements.
-- src:1079 | 2 A provision of an amending law inserts a section that is divided into paragraphs. The paragraphs may be given separate commencements.
@ref s 78 (1), examples (src:1077-1079)
GIVEN thingInsertedByTheProvision IS A STRING
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 78 (1), examples: the things inserted by the provision may be given separate commencements` MEANS
    IF   elem thingInsertedByTheProvision (LIST "2 sections", "the paragraphs of a section divided into paragraphs")
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:1085 | (2) This section applies to a law unless it is displaced by, or under authority given by, an Act or, if the postponed law is a subordinate law or disallowable instrument, the postponed law.
@ref s 79 (2) (src:1085-1085)
GIVEN displacedByOrUnderAuthorityGivenByAnAct IS A BOOLEAN, thePostponedLawIsASubordinateLawOrDisallowableInstrumentAndIsDisplacedByThatLaw IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 79 (2): s 79 applies to the law` MEANS NOT (displacedByOrUnderAuthorityGivenByAnAct OR thePostponedLawIsASubordinateLawOrDisallowableInstrumentAndIsDisplacedByThatLaw)

-- src:1090 | law means an Act, subordinate law, disallowable instrument or notifiable instrument.
@ref s 79 (4), definition of law (src:1090-1090)
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of Act or instrument`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 79 (4): the kind of document is a law for s 79` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `an Act` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a subordinate law` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a disallowable instrument` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a notifiable instrument` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a commencement notice` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a statutory instrument of another kind` THEN FALSE

-- src:1092 | notification day, for a postponed law, means the notification day of—
-- src:1093 | (a) if the postponed law is a law—the law; or
-- src:1094 | (b) if the postponed law is a provision of a law—the law that enacts the provision.
@ref s 79 (4), definition of notification day, for a postponed law (src:1092-1094)
GIVEN thePostponedLawIsALaw IS A BOOLEAN, notificationDayOfThatLaw IS A DATE, notificationDayOfTheLawThatEnactsTheProvision IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 79 (4): the notification day of the postponed law` MEANS
    IF   thePostponedLawIsALaw
    THEN notificationDayOfThatLaw
    ELSE notificationDayOfTheLawThatEnactsTheProvision

-- src:1095 | postponed law means a law that does not commence on its notification day because a law postpones its commencement until a day or time fixed or determined by a commencement notice.
@ref s 79 (4), definition of postponed law (src:1095-1095)
GIVEN theLawDoesNotCommenceOnItsNotificationDay IS A BOOLEAN, aLawPostponesItsCommencementUntilADayOrTimeFixedOrDeterminedByACommencementNotice IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 79 (4): the law is a postponed law` MEANS
    theLawDoesNotCommenceOnItsNotificationDay AND aLawPostponesItsCommencementUntilADayOrTimeFixedOrDeterminedByACommencementNotice

-- src:1098 | (1) This section applies if a law (the amending law) amends a law that has not commenced (the uncommenced law).
@ref s 79A (1) (src:1098-1098)
GIVEN aLawAmendsAnotherLaw IS A BOOLEAN, theAmendedLawHasNotCommenced IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 79A (1): s 79A applies to the amending law` MEANS aLawAmendsAnotherLaw AND theAmendedLawHasNotCommenced

-- src:1099 | (2) The amendment of the uncommenced law does not of itself commence that law.
@ref s 79A (2) (src:1099-1099)
GIVEN s79AApplies IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 79A (2): the amendment of the uncommenced law of itself commences that law` MEANS
    IF   s79AApplies
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:1100 | (3) The amendment made by the amending law commences on the commencement of the uncommenced law.
@ref s 79A (3) (src:1100-1100)
GIVEN s79AApplies IS A BOOLEAN, commencementOfTheUncommencedLaw IS A `Point in time`
GIVETH A MAYBE `Point in time`
`s 79A (3): when the amendment made by the amending law commences` MEANS
    IF   s79AApplies
    THEN JUST commencementOfTheUncommencedLaw
    ELSE NOTHING

DECLARE `What a reference to the commencement of a law is a reference to` IS ONE OF
    `the commencement of the remaining provisions of the law concerned`
    `the commencement of the provision containing the reference`
    `the commencement of the relevant provision of the law concerned`

-- src:1105 | In a law, a reference to the commencement of the law, or another law, (the law concerned) is a reference to—
-- src:1106 | (a) if the provisions of the law concerned (other than those providing for its name and commencement) commence, or are required to commence, on a single day or at a single time—the commencement of the remaining provisions; or
-- src:1107 | (b) if paragraph (a) does not apply and the reference is in a provision of the law concerned—the commencement of the provision; or
-- src:1108 | (c) in any other case—the commencement of the relevant provision of the law concerned.
@ref s 80 (src:1105-1108)
GIVEN theProvisionsOtherThanThoseProvidingForNameAndCommencementCommenceOnASingleDayOrAtASingleTime IS A BOOLEAN, theReferenceIsInAProvisionOfTheLawConcerned IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `What a reference to the commencement of a law is a reference to`
`s 80: what a reference to the commencement of the law concerned is a reference to` MEANS
    IF   theProvisionsOtherThanThoseProvidingForNameAndCommencementCommenceOnASingleDayOrAtASingleTime
    THEN `the commencement of the remaining provisions of the law concerned`
    ELSE IF   theReferenceIsInAProvisionOfTheLawConcerned
         THEN `the commencement of the provision containing the reference`
         ELSE `the commencement of the relevant provision of the law concerned`

-- src:1111 | (1) This section applies to a power to make an appointment or statutory instrument, or to do anything else, in the following situations:
-- src:1112 | (a) the power is given by a law (the authorising law) that has been notified but has not commenced;
-- src:1113 | (b) the power is given by a law (the authorising law) as amended by another law (the amending law) and the laws have been notified, but all or any of them have not commenced.
@ref s 81 (1) (src:1111-1113)
GIVEN theAuthorisingLawHasBeenNotifiedButHasNotCommenced IS A BOOLEAN, theAuthorisingLawAsAmendedByTheAmendingLawHasBeenNotifiedButAllOrAnyOfThemHaveNotCommenced IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 81 (1): s 81 applies to the power` MEANS
    theAuthorisingLawHasBeenNotifiedButHasNotCommenced OR theAuthorisingLawAsAmendedByTheAmendingLawHasBeenNotifiedButAllOrAnyOfThemHaveNotCommenced

-- src:1114 | Examples—powers to which section applies
-- src:1115 | 1 power to delegate a function
-- src:1116 | 2 power to give or issue an approval, consent, licence, permit or other authority (however described)
-- src:1117 | 3 power to make an acting appointment
-- src:1118 | 4 power to issue guidelines
@ref s 81 (1), examples (powers to which section applies) (src:1114-1118)
GIVEN power IS A STRING
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 81 (1), examples: the power is one to which s 81 applies` MEANS
    IF   elem power (LIST "power to delegate a function", "power to give or issue an approval, consent, licence, permit or other authority (however described)", "power to make an acting appointment", "power to issue guidelines")
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:1119 | (2) To remove any doubt and without limiting subsection (1), this section applies to any of the following powers if the power is to be exercised in relation to an entity to be established by the authorising law or the authorising law as amended by the amending law:
-- src:1120 | (a) a power to make an appointment to the entity;
-- src:1121 | (b) a power to make a statutory instrument for the purposes of the entity;
-- src:1122 | (c) a power to do anything else in relation to the entity.
-- src:1123 | Example
-- src:1124 | This section applies to powers under an authorising law to be exercised in relation to the conduct of an election for members of a board to be established as a corporation by the authorising law.
@ref s 81 (2) (src:1119-1124)
GIVEN thePowerIsToBeExercisedInRelationToAnEntityToBeEstablishedByTheAuthorisingLaw IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 81 (2): s 81 applies to the power to make an appointment, make a statutory instrument or do anything else in relation to the entity` MEANS
    IF   thePowerIsToBeExercisedInRelationToAnEntityToBeEstablishedByTheAuthorisingLaw
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:1125 | (3) The power may be exercised at any time even though the authorising law, or the authorising law and amending law (or either of them), is not in force at the time.
@ref s 81 (3) (src:1125-1125)
GIVEN s81Applies IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 81 (3): the power may be exercised at any time even though the authorising law is not in force` MEANS
    IF   s81Applies
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:1126 | (4) For the exercise of the power, the authorising law, or the authorising law and amending law, are taken to be in force at the time of the exercise of the power.
@ref s 81 (4) (src:1126-1126)
GIVEN s81Applies IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 81 (4): the authorising law is taken to be in force at the time of the exercise of the power` MEANS
    IF   s81Applies
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:1127 | (5) Also, anything else may be done under the power at any time for the purpose of bringing, or in relation to bringing, the authorising law, or the authorising law as amended by the amending law, into operation.
@ref s 81 (5) (src:1127-1127)
GIVEN s81Applies IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 81 (5): anything else may be done under the power at any time for the purpose of bringing the authorising law into operation` MEANS
    IF   s81Applies
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:1134 | (8) In the application of this section to a statutory instrument that is not a legislative instrument, a reference to the instrument being notified is a reference to the instrument being made or, if it is required under an Act or statutory instrument to be approved (however described) by the Executive, a Minister or any other entity, to the instrument being approved.
@ref s 81 (8) (src:1134-1134)
GIVEN `day made` IS A DATE, `day approved, if approval is required` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 81 (8): the day a statutory instrument that is not a legislative instrument is taken to be notified` MEANS
    `s 73 (4) (a): the day a statutory instrument that is not a legislative instrument is made or approved` `day made` `day approved, if approval is required`
